<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan FGEP group buys 54,000 tonnes US corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan FGEP group buys 54,000 tonnes US corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's FGEP corn-buying group bought one 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn from Marubeni at a tender on Friday, local traders said.  </p>
<p>The FGEP group comprises Fwu Sow Grain, Great Wall Enterprise, President Enterprise, Ever Smile Feed Mill Co and new group member Fong Yu Co.</p>
<p>The shipment's freight was fixed with MIT on a FOB basis at US$23.28 per tonne.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p> Shipment Tonne   Date/Location		Price/Future</p>
<p>			U.S. Gulf of Mexico</p>
<p>   One    27,000  March 10 - March 25	US$115.89</p>
<p>	    27,000  March 10 - March 25	38.75 US cents/March</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
